    {
      "id": "privacy.no-error-reporting", "name": "Turn off Windows Error Reporting", "category": "Privacy",
      "impact": "privacy", "benefit": "documented", "summary": "Windows stops creating and sending crash reports.",
      "description": "Turns Windows Error Reporting off for every user of this PC, so Windows no longer creates problem reports after a program crashes or stops responding and no longer sends them to Microsoft. A privacy choice: it doesn't make anything faster.",
      "risk": "systemConfiguration", "valueBasis": "documented", "activation": "immediate",
      "limitations": "Crash reports are how Microsoft and app makers find and fix crashes, and Windows stops offering a known solution after one. Crash dumps you configure yourself (LocalDumps) are a separate setting. A Group Policy can override it. Read on PC-000: already set.",
      "source": "Microsoft Learn 'WER Settings': HKLM\\Software\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Windows Error Reporting\\Disabled, a DWORD, 0 = enabled (default), 1 = disabled ('Enable or disable WER'). A commercial tweak utility offers 'Disable Error Reporting' (its script isn't available). Added in the 2026-10-25 audit follow-up.",
