      "activation": "signOut",
      "requires": [
        "proEdition"
      ],
      "limitations": "Microsoft states that users may still see suggestions for Microsoft features, apps and services, so this does not remove all suggestions (the existing 'No tips, suggestions and promoted apps' entry covers more of those). Microsoft's Policy CSP page lists Pro, Enterprise and Education for this policy and does not list Home, so Home is expected to ignore it. In Intune the policy shows a dependency on the spotlight policy; that is a UI dependency in the CSP, not a registry requirement. Only the signed-in user's hive is written; other users are unaffected. Nothing is measured here; this is about what is shown, not performance.",
      "source": "Microsoft Policy CSP Experience page: AllowThirdPartySuggestionsInWindowsSpotlight maps to group policy 'Do not suggest third-party content in Windows spotlight', registry Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CloudContent value DisableThirdPartySuggestions, User scope, default 1 (allowed), 0 = not allowed, editions Pro/Enterprise/Education, Windows 10 1607+. https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/client-management/mdm/policy-csp-experience ; Windows spotlight configuration page confirms the policy is part of the spotlight policy list: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/configuration/windows-spotlight/",
