      "benefit": "preference",
      "valueBasis": "documented",
      "activation": "immediate",
      "limitations": "Edge will show 'Managed by your organization'. You also lose useful assistance prompts, not only promotions. Microsoft's page marks this policy as not applying to a profile signed in with a Microsoft account, so it may have no effect there; check edge://policy. Supported from Edge 89. Microsoft documents registry-based Edge policy for domain-joined or Intune-enrolled devices; on a standalone PC confirm it is applied.",
      "source": "Microsoft Learn, Edge policy ShowRecommendationsEnabled: controls in-browser assistance notifications ('dialog boxes, flyouts, coach marks and banners'); 'If you disable this setting, users won't receive any recommendations or notifications from Microsoft Edge'; REG_DWORD, Edge 89+. PromotionalTabsEnabled page: 'deprecated - use ShowRecommendationsEnabled instead'.",
