    {
      "id": "power.cpu-ramp-up-fast-ac",
      "name": "Jump to top processor speed when load rises (on AC)",
      "category": "Power",
      "impact": "power",
      "summary": "Windows picks the highest processor performance state when load increases, on AC.",
      "description": "Sets the processor performance increase policy to 2 on AC power. Microsoft defines this value as selecting the highest speed/power performance state when the ideal state is higher than the current one, instead of the ideal state (0) or one step towards it (1). Windows' built-in High performance plan uses 2; Balanced uses 0 on the Windows 11 build 26200 test PC.",
