    {
      "id": "power.power-throttling-off",
      "name": "Turn off power throttling (policy)",
      "category": "Performance",
      "impact": "performance",
      "summary": "Windows stops limiting CPU speed for background apps.",
      "description": "Turns on the 'Turn off Power Throttling' machine policy value. Power throttling puts apps that run in the background on the CPU's most efficient operating modes; Microsoft says it saves up to 11% CPU power and is always engaged unless the Power mode slider is set to Best performance. With the value set, Windows no longer throttles background apps.",
      "risk": "systemConfiguration",
      "level": "safe",
      "benefit": "unverified",
      "valueBasis": "documented",
      "activation": "reboot",
      "minBuild": 19041,
      "requires": [
        "noBattery",
        "proEdition"
      ],
      "limitations": "Meant for desktops: throttling exists to save battery, and this switch applies on battery too, so it isn't offered on PCs with a battery. Background work then runs at normal speed, which uses more power and can compete with a game for CPU time; Microsoft documents what the switch does but no measurement here shows it makes anything faster. Microsoft lists the policy for Pro, Enterprise, Education and IoT Enterprise (Windows 10 2004 with KB5005101 and later, Windows 11), so Home is excluded. On Windows 11 the Power mode slider on Best performance already opts every app out. Absence of the value means users control the setting (Windows default).",
      "source": "Microsoft Learn Policy CSP ADMX_Power 'PowerThrottlingTurnOff' (Turn off Power Throttling, Power.admx): key System\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Power\\PowerThrottling, value PowerThrottlingOff, enabled = throttling off, not configured = users control; editions and builds as stated. Data value 1 (32-bit DWORD) and 'delete to re-enable' from two community guides (Winaero, Maketecheasier). Microsoft Learn 'Customize the Windows performance power slider' says throttling saves up to 11% CPU power and is bypassed on Best performance.",
      "sources": [
        "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/client-management/mdm/policy-csp-admx-power",
        "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-hardware/customize/desktop/customize-power-slider",
        "https://winaero.com/disable-power-throttling-windows-10-1709",
        "https://maketecheasier.com/disable-power-throttling-windows10"
      ],
      "registry": [
        {
          "hive": "HKLM",
          "path": "SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Power\\PowerThrottling",
          "name": "PowerThrottlingOff",
          "type": "dword",
          "value": "1"
        }
      ]
    },
