      "name": "Turn off window animations (policy)",
      "category": "Appearance",
      "impact": "interface",
      "summary": "Stops the minimise, maximise and restore animations of windows.",
      "description": "Sets the Desktop Window Manager policy 'Do not allow window animations'. Windows then skips the animation played when a window is restored, minimised or maximised, so the window changes state at once. Microsoft documents that the policy takes effect after the user signs out and back in. Microsoft describes it only for window restore, minimise and maximise animations.",
