      "limitations": "A look-and-feel change only; Microsoft documents no performance effect and Mesura does not claim one. Overlaps with the existing 'minimise animation' entry (that one is the per-user MinAnimate setting; this is the DWM policy). Microsoft lists the policy for Pro, Enterprise and Education, so Windows Home is treated as not applicable (proEdition). It takes effect at the next sign-in. How the animation switches in Settings behave while the policy is set was not tested. Windows default: not configured (animations on).",
      "source": "Microsoft Learn Policy CSP ADMX_DWM: policy 'Do not allow window animations' (DwmDisallowAnimations_1, User scope; key SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\DWM, value DisallowAnimations; 'If you enable this policy setting, window animations are turned off'; 'Changing this policy setting requires a logoff'; Windows 11 21H2 and later, Pro/Enterprise/Education). The DWORD type and enabled value 1 were read from DWM.admx in C:\\Windows\\PolicyDefinitions on Windows 11 build 26200 (enabledValue decimal 1, disabledValue decimal 0).",
