    {
      "id": "gaming.game-recording-policy-off",
      "name": "Disallow Windows Game Recording and Broadcasting (policy)",
      "category": "Graphics",
      "impact": "performance",
      "summary": "Machine-wide policy that blocks Game Bar recording and broadcasting.",
      "description": "Sets the documented AllowGameDVR policy to 0, which tells Windows not to allow Windows Game Recording and Broadcasting for any user. It is the machine-wide, documented form of turning off Game Bar captures; the per-user catalog entries use community-documented values instead. Microsoft states that if the setting is enabled or not configured, recording and broadcasting are allowed (the default).",
