      "limitations": "Game Bar recording and broadcasting stop being allowed for every user until the policy is removed. Microsoft's performance effect is not documented: Windows ships with background recording off, so the saving is nil unless recording had been turned on. Microsoft's page notes the policy is 'only enforced in Windows 10 for desktop'; enforcement on Windows 11 is not spelled out, and a registry read-back confirms the value but not the behaviour. Whether Game Bar screenshots are affected is not documented. Ignored by Windows Home (proEdition). Windows default: not configured (allowed).",
      "source": "Microsoft Learn Policy CSP ApplicationManagement/AllowGameDVR: 'This setting enables or disables the Windows Game Recording and Broadcasting features. If you disable this setting, Windows Game Recording won't be allowed. If the setting is enabled or not configured, then Recording and Broadcasting (streaming) will be allowed'; 0 = Not allowed, 1 = Allowed (default); Device scope; Pro/Enterprise/Education; Windows 10 1507 and later; Group Policy 'Enables or disables Windows Game Recording and Broadcasting', key Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\GameDVR, value AllowGameDVR. GameDVR.admx on Windows 11 build 26200 confirms the same key/value with enabledValue decimal 1 and disabledValue decimal 0.",
