      "category": "Appearance",
      "impact": "interface",
      "summary": "Enables Per-Process System DPI so some blurry apps turn sharp after a restart.",
      "description": "Enables the Windows policy 'Configure Per-Process System DPI settings'. After the scale of the primary display changes (connecting or disconnecting a monitor with another scale, a remote session, or changing the scale), many older desktop apps stay blurry until you sign out. With the policy on, some of them become sharp after the app is restarted, without signing out.",
