    {
      "id": "gaming.controller-game-bar-off",
      "name": "Don't open Game Bar from the controller's Xbox button",
      "category": "Graphics",
      "impact": "interface",
      "summary": "Stops the Xbox/Guide button on a controller from opening Game Bar.",
      "description": "Turns off Settings > Gaming > Game Bar > 'Allow your controller to open Game Bar'. Microsoft's Windows 11 settings reference names the value (UseNexusForGameBarEnabled, REG_DWORD, 0 or 1) as the key behind that toggle; community guides and a Microsoft Q&A answer agree that 0 is off. It prevents Game Bar from popping up over a game when the controller button is pressed by accident.",
      "risk": "userPreference",
      "level": "safe",
      "benefit": "preference",
      "valueBasis": "community",
      "activation": "reboot",
      "limitations": "Only the controller shortcut is removed; Win+G and the Game Bar app itself are untouched. Microsoft documents the value only as the key behind this toggle and does not say which of 0 or 1 is on. The 0 = off direction comes from a Microsoft Q&A answer and community guides. The default is disputed (a Windows 10 tutorial says on, a Windows 11 tutorial says off), and the value is absent on a fresh profile such as this research PC. On a Windows 11 PC where it is already off, applying it changes nothing. A Q&A answer says to restart Windows afterwards. Undo restores the recorded before-image (a deleted value if it was absent). Brings no documented performance change; it is an interface preference.",
      "source": "Microsoft Learn, Reference for Windows 11 settings > Gaming: HKCU\\Software\\Microsoft\\GameBar, UseNexusForGameBarEnabled, REG_DWORD 0 or 1, 'Key associated with toggle Gaming -> Game Bar -> Allow your controller to open Game Bar' (https://learn.microsoft.com/windows/apps/develop/settings/settings-windows-11). Microsoft Q&A answer (community) sets it to 0 to stop the controller button opening Game Bar and says to restart (https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/answers/questions/5892017/need-to-prevent-gamebar-from-opening-ever-under-an). 0 = off is community-established (Ten Forums/Eleven Forum tutorials seen only as search snippets; pages returned 403). Default is disputed between those tutorials.",
      "sources": [
        "https://learn.microsoft.com/windows/apps/develop/settings/settings-windows-11",
        "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/answers/questions/5892017/need-to-prevent-gamebar-from-opening-ever-under-an"
      ],
      "registry": [
        {
