      "source": "Microsoft Learn 'Detect, enable, and disable SMBv1, SMBv2, and SMBv3': 'SMBv1 has significant security vulnerabilities, and we strongly encourage you not to use it'; Disable-WindowsOptionalFeature -FeatureName SMB1Protocol; restart; not installed by default in Windows 11. Microsoft Learn 'SMBv1 Not Installed by Default': deprecated 2014; Windows 10 Home/Pro clean installs: client present by default until unused 15 days (Pro no longer from 1809); error text when a device needs SMB1; Computer Browser removed with SMB1. I could not run Get-WindowsOptionalFeature (needs elevation), so the feature name is from Microsoft's page, not from this PC.",
