      ],
      "limitations": "Themes, saved Wi-Fi/password data, language and other preferences no longer follow your Microsoft account to your other PCs, and a new PC will not receive them from this one. Settings shows the option as managed by your organisation. Group Policy values: Microsoft lists them for Pro, Enterprise and Education, so on Home they may be ignored. Sync built into Edge or other apps is a separate setting and is not changed. Microsoft's pages call the UI 'Sync your settings' and, on newer Windows 11 builds, 'Windows backup'; which Settings page is switched off on every build was not checked. Windows default: sync on and user-controlled (values absent).",
      "source": "Microsoft Learn 'Manage connections from Windows operating system components to Microsoft services' item 21: HKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\SettingSync DisableSettingSync = 2 and DisableSettingSyncUserOverride = 1 (Group Policy 'Do not sync', 'Allow users to turn syncing on' left unchecked). Policy CSP ADMX_SettingSync 'DisableSettingSync': enabling turns 'sync your settings' off so none of the groups is synced; Pro/Enterprise/Education, Windows 10 2004+ and Windows 11. The local SettingSync.admx (Windows 11 build 26200) confirms enabledValue 2 and that the unchecked 'Allow users...' box writes DisableSettingSyncUserOverride = 1.",
      "sources": [
        "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/privacy/manage-connections-from-windows-operating-system-components-to-microsoft-services",
        "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/client-management/mdm/policy-csp-admx-settingsync",
        "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/client-management/mdm/policy-csp-experience"
      ],
      "registry": [
        {
          "hive": "HKLM",
          "path": "SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\SettingSync",
          "name": "DisableSettingSync",
          "type": "dword",
          "value": "2"
        },
        {
          "hive": "HKLM",
          "path": "SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\SettingSync",
          "name": "DisableSettingSyncUserOverride",
          "type": "dword",
          "value": "1"
        }
      ]
    },
