    {
      "id": "edge.sleeping-tabs-on",
      "name": "Keep Edge sleeping tabs turned on",
      "category": "Microsoft Edge",
      "impact": "performance",
      "summary": "Locks sleeping tabs on so idle background tabs release CPU and memory.",
      "description": "Sleeping tabs puts idle background tabs to sleep to reduce CPU, battery and memory use; Microsoft says Edge uses heuristics to avoid sleeping tabs that do useful work such as notifications, sound or video. Microsoft states sleeping tabs is on by default. This sets the Edge policy SleepingTabsEnabled to 1, so the feature stays on and users cannot switch it off.",
