      "limitations": "Microsoft: after you disable WPAD you must configure every proxy manually, so do not use it on a work or school network that hands out proxy settings automatically. It only covers WinHTTP; Microsoft says to also turn off 'Automatically detect settings' in Settings, because browsers and third-party apps use that setting (not changed here, it is a per-user setting stored in a binary blob). 'nslookup wpad' still resolves, because apps can still query DNS directly. Microsoft's own service guidance marks the WinHTTP Web Proxy Auto-Discovery service 'Do not disable', so the service itself is left alone. Applies from Windows 10 1809. No speed gain is claimed.",
      "source": "Microsoft Learn 'How to disable HTTP proxy features': 'Starting in Windows Server 2019 and Windows 10, version 1809, you can disable WPAD by setting a DWORD value ... HKLM\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Internet Settings\\WinHttp\\DisableWpad to 1'; manual proxy configuration needed afterwards; WPAD should also be disabled in the Settings UI; nslookup WPAD still resolves. 'Security guidelines for system services': WinHttpAutoProxySvc 'Do not disable'. The value is absent on this Windows 11 PC.",
      "sources": [
