        "proEdition"
      ],
      "limitations": "You cannot locate, lock or recover a lost or stolen laptop or tablet from account.microsoft.com, which is what the feature is for; desktops rarely benefit from it. Group Policy value: Pro, Enterprise and Education, Windows 10 1703+. Windows default: allowed (value absent). A device that is already registered is expected to stop being locatable, but Microsoft's page does not say whether an existing cloud record is removed.",
      "source": "Microsoft Learn Policy CSP Experience 'AllowFindMyDevice': when on, 'the device and its location are registered in the cloud'; when off, 'the device and its location aren't registered and the Find My Device feature won't work'; 0 = not allowed, 1 (default) = allowed; Group Policy 'Turn On/Off Find My Device', key SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\FindMyDevice, value AllowFindMyDevice (FindMy.admx), Windows 10 1703+. Learn 'Manage connections...' item 5 gives HKLM\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\FindMyDevice\\AllowFindMyDevice = 0.",
      "sources": [
        "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/client-management/mdm/policy-csp-experience",
        "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/privacy/manage-connections-from-windows-operating-system-components-to-microsoft-services"
