    {
      "id": "edge.hide-first-run",
      "name": "Skip the Edge first-run experience",
      "category": "Microsoft Edge",
      "impact": "interface",
      "summary": "Edge skips the first-run screens and splash screen for new profiles.",
      "description": "This sets the Edge policy HideFirstRunExperience to 1, so the first-run experience and splash screen are not shown when Edge runs for the first time. Microsoft lists the defaults it then uses: the new tab feed is MSN News with the Inspirational layout, a Windows Azure AD or Microsoft account is still signed in automatically, and sync is not enabled by default (the user is asked at startup).",
