      "limitations": "Edge will show 'Managed by your organization'. It only matters for a profile that has not yet run Edge for the first time; Microsoft describes it as applying at first run, so it is not expected to change an existing, already set-up profile. Needs an Edge restart. You skip the choices the first-run screen offers (import, feed type, sync), so they must be set later in Settings. Supported from Edge 80.",
      "source": "Microsoft Learn, Edge policy HideFirstRunExperience: 'If you enable this policy, the First-run experience and the splash screen won't be shown to users when they run Microsoft Edge for the first time'; lists resulting defaults (MSN News feed, Inspirational layout, sync prompt); REG_DWORD, Edge 80+; restart required.",
      "sources": [
