      "id": "memory.compression-off",
      "name": "Turn off memory compression",
      "category": "System",
      "impact": "performance",
      "summary": "Stops Windows compressing rarely used memory pages.",
      "description": "Runs Disable-MMAgent -MemoryCompression. Memory compression keeps pages that haven't been used for a while compressed in RAM instead of writing them to the page file; turning it off makes Windows page them out sooner instead.",
      "risk": "systemConfiguration",
      "level": "moderate",
      "benefit": "unverified",
      "valueBasis": "documented",
      "activation": "reboot",
      "minBuild": 14393,
      "limitations": "Microsoft documents the cmdlet and the switch but states no effect, default or measured benefit, so none is claimed here. It trades some CPU time for RAM: on a PC with little memory, turning it off tends to mean more paging to disk. Takes effect after a restart. Reading and changing it needs administrator rights.",
      "source": "Microsoft Learn: Disable-MMAgent / Enable-MMAgent (MMAgent module). The switch exists and is documented; its effect is not quantified.",
      "sources": [
        "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/powershell/module/mmagent/disable-mmagent",
        "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/powershell/module/mmagent/enable-mmagent"
